{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Vision Encoder Patches Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `PatchEmbed`, an `nn.Module` wrapping `Conv2d` for patch projection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `sinusoidal_2d(grid_h, grid_w, dim)`, a stateless function that builds the 2D position table."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `VisionFrontEnd`, which composes patch embedding, CLS prepend, and position addition into one forward pass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A `synthesize_image(seed)` helper that builds a deterministic 224x224x3 fixture from `numpy.random`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that runs one fixture image through the front end and prints the output shape, the CLS token norm, and one row of the position embedding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: the 224x224 fixture is tokenized to a sequence of shape `(1, 197, 768)`. The first token is the CLS; the next 196 are patch tokens. The position embedding norms are uniform within a row, which is the sinusoidal signature."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Replace the sinusoidal position with a learned `nn.Parameter` and compare the first-epoch loss on a tiny synthetic classification task. Learned positions win at fixed resolution; sinusoidal wins when you change resolution after training.\n\n2. Swap the `Conv2d` for an explicit `nn.Unfold` plus `nn.Linear` and assert the outputs match to within float tolerance. Same math, two ways to spell it.\n\n3. Add support for non-square patch sizes (e.g. 32x16 for wide-aspect inputs) and verify the position table handles non-square grids.\n\n4. Profile the patch step at batch sizes 1, 8, 64. The patch projection is rarely the bottleneck; the attention layers downstream dominate.\n\n5. Train the front end as a frozen feature extractor on a 4-class synthetic shape dataset (circles, squares, triangles, stars). The CLS token output should linearly separate."
      ]
    }
  ],
